<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Annexation of the Punjab</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1849">1849</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The annexation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> was the incorporation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a>'s territory into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> in 1849. It followed British victory in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-anglo-sikh-war">Second Anglo-Sikh War</a>. The young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duleep-singh">Maharaja Duleep Singh</a> was deposed, ending the Sikh Empire.</p></div>
